# Playable build version (required)

Players must always know which build they are running. Merging to GitHub does **not** update a laptop still running an old `serve.mjs` — agents must leave the tree so `node playable/refresh.mjs` always yields the new BUILD label.

## Source of truth
- `playable/package.json` → `"version"` is the only version number to edit.
- UI imports `APP_VERSION` / `APP_BUILD_LABEL` from `playable/src/version.ts` (Vite bakes version + git sha at build time).
- `playable/dist/build-info.json` is written on every production build. Do **not** hand-edit it.
- Do **not** hardcode `0.x.y` strings in HUD, menus, or copy.

## On every playable change that players can notice
1. Bump `playable/package.json` version (patch for fixes/polish, minor for larger features).
2. Keep the root `README.md` title line version in sync (`Painted Abyss — First Dive · x.y.z`).
3. Keep the on-screen `BUILD v… · <sha>` badge visible on the **menu and during the dive**. Do not remove it or the stale-tab warning.
4. Run `npm run build` in `playable/` and **commit the updated `playable/dist/`** (including `build-info.json`) so `serve.mjs` / `refresh.mjs` match GitHub without an extra local rebuild dependency.
5. Mention the new version in the PR summary so playtesters know what to look for.

## Serving / playtest (tell humans this)
- After any agent merges: on the Mac run `node playable/refresh.mjs` (pulls `main`, kills port 5173, rebuilds, serves).
- Or: kill old server, `git pull`, then `node playable/serve.mjs` (auto-rebuilds if `dist` version ≠ `package.json`).
- Terminal must print `Painted Abyss vX.Y.Z · <sha> ready`.
- UI must show the same `BUILD vX.Y.Z · <sha>`. If a yellow **OUTDATED TAB** banner appears, hard-refresh or re-run `refresh.mjs`.

## Generated stamp conflicts
`playable/dist/**` (`build-info.json` `sha` / `builtAt`, `index.html`, hashed bundles) and `docs/verification/physics-reality.json` `generatedAt` are baked. Two playable PRs will always disagree on those lines. Do **not** edit them to resolve a conflict, and do **not** keep either side's `sha`, `builtAt`, or `generatedAt`.

1. `node playable/rematch-dist.mjs` — drops conflicted `playable/dist` and regenerates `physics-reality.json` by re-running its test. Source conflicts are left for you.
2. Fix remaining source conflicts. Bump `playable/package.json` past `origin/main`.
3. Commit the merge (source only; dist may be absent).
4. `node playable/rematch-dist.mjs --bake` — runs `npm run build`, which writes a new `build-info.json`. Commit the staged `playable/dist`. The baked `sha` must be the merge commit from step 3.
5. Push and confirm the PR is MERGEABLE. If `origin/main` moved, repeat from step 1.

## Do not
- Leave a playable PR without bumping the version.
- Ship source-only changes without rebuilding `dist`.
- Hand-pick `sha`, `builtAt`, or `generatedAt` out of a conflict.
- Assume the player's already-open Safari tab updates when GitHub updates — it does not.
